      en: "Ap Chau (Round Island) is a small island in northeastern Hong Kong, in Yan Chau Tong Marine Park. The island is about 300 m in diameter and known for its round granite rock that forms a flat platform at the top. The island is uninhabited and popular with kayakers and snorkelers. The surrounding water is rich in marine life. The name 'Ap Chau' means 'Duck Island' in Cantonese. The island is part of Plover Cove Country Park. It is accessible only by boat, often from Lai Chi Wo. The island features unique geology with red sandstone rocks.",
